---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Credits"
  description="Attribution for recipe ideas from local.sybilsolutions.ai / 0xSero, the house test-rig work, and Shannon’s cited lab write-up."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <p class="kicker">Attribution</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Credits</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      AMDai is independent. Product names belong to their owners. Numbers on this site are either measured on our test rig or labeled.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Sybil Local AI registry</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The idea of a <strong class="text-ink">recipe</strong> — one exact launch of model X on GPU Y, with proof it worked —
        comes from the
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="https://local.sybilsolutions.ai">Sybil Local AI registry</a>
        by <strong class="text-ink">0xSero</strong>
        (<a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="https://github.com/sybil-solutions/local-ai-registry">sybil-solutions/local-ai-registry</a>).
        That project is MIT-licensed, © 2026 0xSero.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We did <strong class="text-ink">not</strong> import their AMD card files or their recipe proofs on this ship.
        We re-implemented the idea in our own words and Astro pages: evidence tiers, a pass/fail suite,
        a static JSON API, withdrawals, and a contribute path.
        Their site’s prose and UI code stay theirs.
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-line bg-raised p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed"><code>{`MIT License

Copyright (c) 2026 0xSero

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
copies or substantial portions of the Software.`}</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">
        Full license text lives upstream. If we later ingest their AMD Q4+ rows, each cell will say
        “Cited external” and link the recipe file. That import is a separate task.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">local desktop / our test rig</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Official test-run cards on <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/results">/results</a>
        are credited to AMDai (verified, local desktop). Schema <code>amdai-bench/run@1</code>.
        Official 2026-10-13 set: 35B UD-Q5_K_XL 102.39 / 90.52 / 66.43 / 44.4, Q5_K_M 109.73,
        Q4_K_M 117.69, Q6_K 103.23 at 4K, dual split 82.78 at 4K / 42.03 at 256K,
        dual-instance ~100 / 172 / ~177. Flash / Strata / Q3 are pending a DDR5 rerun.
        Label: Measured on our rig, 2026-10.
        A measured Qwen 3.8 Flash Q3 run is an approved one-time exception — it will show as measured when the jsonl line lands.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Shannon / @iamMrDuncan</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The community lab write-up on
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/labs/shannon">/labs/shannon</a>
        is sourced from Shannon (@iamMrDuncan), X Article
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="https://x.com/iamMrDuncan/status/2109744566001938923" rel="noopener">How I run my Lab</a>
        (2026-10-12). Every claim there is labeled
        <strong class="text-ink">Cited, not measured by AMDai</strong>.
        We did not invent tok/s, prices, or a Thermite repo URL.
        Herdr and Coolify appear in
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="/harnesses">/harnesses</a>
        because of that write-up. The P100 Qwen 3.8 27B ~33 tok/s with MTP figure is NVIDIA
        cited context only —
        <a class="underline decoration-accent/40" href="https://x.com/iamMrDuncan/status/2107109051301568582" rel="noopener">Oct 5 post</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
